From: DevOps Hero <doh@devopshero.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] Bedrock TTFT perf telemetry over SSE `perf` event

Pinned upstream: hermes-webui 0.50.259.

Purpose: surface end-to-end and per-segment latency for Bedrock chat turns
to the browser console so we can see whether sluggishness is Bedrock TTFT
or our own pre-Bedrock work. One-shot `perf` SSE event per turn, gated on
provider == 'bedrock'. No UI, no server-side log.

Segments (all in ms, monotonic on their origin host):

  our_stack_ms        — /api/chat/start received → converse_stream() called
  bedrock_ttft_ms     — converse_stream() called → first Bedrock delta
  callback_to_sse_ms  — first Bedrock delta → first `token` on SSE queue

The browser (`static/messages.js`) adds two more numbers for the full
picture:

  post_rtt_ms       — Enter → /api/chat/start POST responded
  browser_ttft_ms   — Enter → first `token` rendered in the chat

The backend timestamps are stashed on the AIAgent instance by
`patches/05-bedrock-ttft-perf.patch`. This patch reads them on first
on_token() and clears them after emission so reused agents (the
SESSION_AGENT_CACHE path) don't report stale numbers on a later turn that
didn't actually hit Bedrock (e.g. tool-only loops).

Upstream status: DOH-specific; no plan to upstream. Revisit if upstream
adds a first-class TTFT metric in api/metering.py.

